    {
      "id": "#/texts/88",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "provider_label": "text",
      "text": "Runtime Characteristics To analyze Docling's runtime characteristics, we begin by exploring the relationship between document length (in pages) and conversion time. As shown in Figure 3, this relationship is not strictly linear, as documents differ in their frequency of tables and bitmap elements (i.e., scanned content). This requires OCR or table structure recognition models to engage dynamically when layout analysis has detected such elements.",
      "raw_text": "Runtime Characteristics To analyze Docling's runtime characteristics, we begin by exploring the relationship between document length (in pages) and conversion time. As shown in Figure 3, this relationship is not strictly linear, as documents differ in their frequency of tables and bitmap elements (i.e., scanned content). This requires OCR or table structure recognition models to engage dynamically when layout analysis has detected such elements.",
      "reading_order": 41,
      "level": 1,
